How to bake a loaf of bread. First, mix four hundred grams of flour with a teaspoon of salt and a teaspoon of dry yeast in a large bowl. Add about three hundred milliliters of warm water and stir until the dough comes together. Turn it out onto a floured surface and knead it for ten minutes, until it is smooth and elastic. Place the dough in a clean bowl, cover it with a damp cloth, and leave it in a warm place for one hour, or until it has doubled in size. Then shape it into a round, set it on a baking tray, and bake it in a hot oven for thirty minutes. The loaf is done when it sounds hollow if you tap the bottom.

